<item ID="1744595943" Creator="Chuck Wade" >
<attribute name="Associates" ></attribute>
<attribute name="Color" >bright blue</attribute>
<attribute name="Created" >2025-02-22T15:01:37+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="DisplayedAttributes" >Subtitle;Modified;Checked;EdictDisabled;RuleDisabled;MyDictionary;ID;Path;OnPaste</attribute>
<attribute name="DominantLanguage" >en</attribute>
<attribute name="Edict" >// To rebuild dictionary, turn $Checked on
if($Checked) { $MyDictionary={};   $Checked=false; }; // Build a lookup dictionary for child notes found in ‘this’ container.
// The resulting dictionary maps $Name values to the corresponding $ID value. 
// In addition, if there are any child Notes in this container named 
// “Code Archive” or “Packages,” then their children will also be included.
// The resulting dictionary is placed into the $MyDictionary attribute
// of this container.

var:string  newLookup; // New Lookup entry for “Document Commons” Dictionary

$ID(children).each(global_note)
{ 
  newLookup=$Name(global_note)+&quot;:&quot;+$ID(global_note);
  $MyDictionary=$MyDictionary.add({newLookup});
  if($Name(global_note)==&quot;Packages&quot;)
  { 
    $ID(children(global_note)).each(package)
    { 
      newLookup=&quot;Package_&quot;+$Name(package)+&quot;:&quot;+$ID(package);
      $MyDictionary=$MyDictionary.add({newLookup});
    }; // End each “Package” loop
  }; // EndIf “Packages” container processing
  if($Name(global_note)==&quot;Code Archive&quot;)
  {
    $ID(children(global_note)).each(code_archive)
    { 
      newLookup=&quot;CodeArchive_&quot;+$Name(code_archive)+&quot;:&quot;+$ID(code_archive);
      $MyDictionary=$MyDictionary.add({newLookup});
    }; // End each “Code Archive” loop
  }; // EndIf “Code Archive” container processing
}; //End of children-of-commons loop
 
// Notes:
// (1) The intended use of the resulting dictionary is to allow other 
// code to easily look up the $IDs of the notes maintained in the 
// common section of the document, which should be the last top-level
// note in the document. Consequently, this dictionary can always be
// accessed as “$MyDictionary(lastSibling(cover))” </attribute>
<attribute name="EdictDisabled" >false</attribute>
<attribute name="HideDisplayedAttributes" >true</attribute>
<attribute name="IsComposite" >false</attribute>
<attribute name="IsSeparator" >true</attribute>
<attribute name="Modified" >2025-04-13T18:30:16+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="MyDictionary" >LogBooks:1744596204;Package_Debugging &amp; Logging Tools:1744661339;Package_Network Tools:1744596513;Package_Package Template:1744596189;Global Settings:1744595944;Packages:1744596012;Package_User Attribute Management:1744596013;Discards:1744596297;Package_Diagram View:1744596449;Document Commons:1744596570;Package_ReadMe “Document Commons Framework for Package Management &amp; Sharing”:1747669950;Document Attributes:1744595946;Copy of “Document Commons”:1744596570</attribute>
<attribute name="NLNames" >User</attribute>
<attribute name="NLPlaces" >Edict</attribute>
<attribute name="Name" >Document Commons</attribute>
<attribute name="OnPaste" >if(!$Checked)
{ require(&quot;Hints&quot;); require(&quot;Prototypes&quot;); require(&quot;Templates&quot;);
  if($Subtitle(lastSibling(cover))!=&quot;Document Commons&quot;)
  { // “Document Commons” container does not exist
    $MyBoolean(&quot;./Essentials&quot;)=false;
    $MyNumber(&quot;./Essentials&quot;)=$ID;
    $Checked(&quot;./Document Attributes&quot;)=true;
    $RuleDisabled=false;
    $Checked=true;
    $EdictDisabled=false;
    $Color=&quot;bright blue&quot;;
  } else 
  { // There is already a “Document Commons” container
    $MyBoolean(&quot;./Essentials&quot;)=true;
    $MyNumber(&quot;./Essentials&quot;)=$ID(lastSibling(cover));
    $Name+=&quot; copy&quot;;
  };
  // Invoke Essentials Installer to complete installation
  $RuleDisabled(&quot;./Essentials&quot;)=false;
}; //Endif not Checked</attribute>
<attribute name="Rule" >// Force this Note to always be the last Top-Level Note // in the Document. if($OutlineOrder!=$OutlineOrder(lastSibling(cover)))
{ // Then this is not the last top-level Note/Container
  // Check that there is not already a lastSibling(cover)
  // with the same name as this note
  if($Name!=$Name(lastSibling(cover)))
  { // Then move this note to its correct position
  create(&quot;/Temp_Gw7WvqP5b_&quot;); // Just a random name, since it willl be tossed
  $Container=&quot;/Temp_Gw7WvqP5b_&quot;;   $Container=&quot;/&quot;;   $Prototype=;   delete(&quot;/Temp_Gw7WvqP5b_&quot;);
  } else
  {
  show(&quot;There is a duplicate &quot;+$Name+&quot; Container—Correct!&quot;,&quot;poppy&quot;,&quot;bright blue&quot;);
  $RuleDisabled=true;
  };
};</attribute>
<attribute name="RuleDisabled" >false</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenHeight" >23</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenWidth" >679</attribute>
<attribute name="SelectionCount" >173</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >-0.5846153979</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >-0.6;-0.6;-0.6;-0.6;-0.6;-0.4;-1;-0.6;0.6;-0.6;-0.6;-1;-1</attribute>
<attribute name="Subtitle" >Document Commons</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >45.5</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >The default name for this container is “Document Commons,” and it is intended to be a consistent repository for settings and information used by automation (e.g., Action code, Stamps, Functions). It also serves as a vehicle for populating a new or existing document with automation packages by merely copying this container into the destination document. For Tinderbox 10.1.2 and later, copying this container into a document will invoke the included $OnPaste code that will, in turn, perform a series of initialization steps to establish the “Document Commons” repository along with some core functionality that can be used to install packages and provide essential automation support functions. The $OnPaste code may be disabled by setting $Checked to true, which can be useful when building a new version of the “Document Commons” container for subsequent export to other documents.
The associated Rule forces this Container to always be the last top-level Note in the Tinderbox document. This allows code to always reference this Container as $Path(lastSibling(cover)) or $ID(lastSibling(cover)) since the “cover” Note is always the first top-level Note. This convention provides a rational place where data used by document automation can be stored, along with relevant documentation, without having to rely on the Name of this container. In other words, users can rename the “Document Commons” container to anything they want, as long as code that relies on this container uses the lastSibling(cover) method for access. This Rule may be disabled by checking the $RuleDisabled box. As an aside, this container is configured to be a Separator, which helps with visual recognition and also prevents this container and its contents from automatically appearing in a Map View.
The $Subtitle of this container should always be set to “Document Commons” to provide a means for testing if the Document Commons has already been installed. Specifically, the test to determine if this already exists is:   if($Subtitle(lastSibling(cover))==&quot;Document Commons&quot;) This method of testing for existence allows the document owner to change the Name of the Document Commons container without breaking the way that code operates.
The associated Edict builds a dictionary in $MyDictionary that maps the names of descendants of this container to their corresponding $ID values. This allows code to always be able to reference named descendants of this container using this lookup: 	$MyDictionary(lastSibling(cover))[commons_name] …where “commons_name” is a string containing just a descendant name located in this container. Note that code does not need to know the name of this “Document Commons” container since it is accessible by its known position in the outline order of the document, and by using this dictionary, code can find places within this container by well-known names. Execution of this Edict can be disabled by checking the $EdictDisabled box or unchecking the “Enabled” box in the Inspector’s Edict pane.
In support of Tinderbox document automation, there are several special child containers that may be located in this “Document Commons” container:
	•	Global Settings: A container where any information that needs to be referenced globally within the Tinderbox document can be maintained. This includes configuration settings used by automation code or add-on packages.
	•	Document Attributes: Copies of User Attributes are maintained as separate notes in this container. These Attribute Notes may be copied to another Tinderbox document where a similarly configured “Document Attributes” container exists, and upon copying, they will be added automatically to the available User Attributes. Optionally, existing User Attributes in the document can be replicated as Attribute Notes within this container.
	•	Essentials: Various items included in this container are used to install some essential features and capabilities that will be available for automation within the Tinderbox document. Add-on packages may also rely on these Essentials.
	•	Packages: A container whose children are expected to be containers relating to specific add-on packages. These package containers will usually include documentation, manifests, and anything else necessary for deploying and using a package. The children of the Packages container will be included in $MyDictionary with their names prefixed with “Package_” so that these package containers can be easily referenced.
	•	Code Archive: In a similar manner to Packages, the Code Archive is expected to be a repository of code building blocks. Normally, these code blocks will not be executed and may be backups of active code located in the “Hints” container. Any children of the Code Archive will be included in $MyDictionary with their names prefixed with “CodeArchive_” to facilitate easy access to these code blocks. The Code Archive is provided in anticipation of forthcoming toolbox packages that will facilitate managing and archiving code within a Tinderbox document. 
	•	LogBooks: This is the repository for any log books used within the document for recording events and providing debugging support. This is used by the “LogRec” function as well as the “Logging” Stamps that are included as “Essentials” with the installation of the “Document Commons” container. 
	•	Discards: When installing add-on packages to a document, any existing items that are replaced by items installed with the package are moved to this Discards container instead of being deleted. This can also be used any time there is an item that should be kept at least temporarily instead of being immediately deleted or removed. 
</text>
