<attribute name="Subtitle" >Essentials</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >48.9</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >-0.1</attribute>
<text >This “Essentials” container provides the items necessary to deploy the “Document Commons” framework into a Tinderbox document, or to update these essential items if previously deployed. The Rule associated with this container will normally be invoked when a “Document Commons” container is pasted into a document. This Rule will then perform the steps necessary to either deploy essential items or update these items if previously deployed. After completing the deployment/update of essential items, this Rule will then invoke the Rule associated with the “Add-on Packages” container, which is a child of this “Essentials” container, and, in turn, the “Add-on Packages” container provides packages that will subsequently be added to the Tinderbox document.
These three System Attributes are used to invoke the “Essentials” Rule and receive necessary context from the “Document Commons” $OnPaste action. 
	•	RuleDisabled: This should always be true, except that when installing a new “Document Commons” container, this will be set to false (by the parent’s $OnPaste action) in order to execute this “Essentials” Rule only once. The Rule invokes the “Installer” action code that is normally the first child of this “Essentials” container. Once all Essential items have been deployed, the Installer will set $RuleDisabled to true so that this Rule will run only once. 
	•	MyBoolean: The “Document Commons” container’s $OnPaste action will set this to true if there is already a “Document Commons” container as the last sibling of the cover. This boolean will be subsequently passed to the “Add-on Packages” container. This allows installer code to deal with the situation where either the “Document Commons” is being installed for the first time in a Tinderbox document, or where it was previously installed and should, therefore, be updated.
	•	MyNumber: The ID of the correct “Document Commons” container. This could either be the parent of this “Essentials” container in the case of a new deployment, or it could be the ID of an already existing “Document Commons.” This ID will be subsequently passed to the “Add-on Packages” container. This allows installers to reference the correct instance of the “Document Commons” container without having to know its actual current Name. 
In addition, this “Essentials” Rule will set $MyString for the “Add-on Packages” container to be the path to the “InstallerLog” where subsequent log messages should be posted.</text>
