<attribute name="Subtitle" >Essentials</attribute>
<attribute name="Width" >3</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >45.5</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >Once an initial Installation of the “Document Commons” essential items is complete, then the “Essentials” Installer will run a secondary installer that is the Rule for this “Add-on Packages” container. This Rule will then examine the other Items in this Container. Each of these items (i.e., “Package Reference” notes) should have the same name as an associated package, as these are intended to act as references to the actual Package. This secondary installer will move each of the referenced packages into the “/Document Commons/Packages” container if they are not already present. If the package does already exist, then the package referenced here will replace it, and the already existing package will be moved to the Discards container.
For each Package Reference Note in this container, the secondary installer will, after ensuring that the Package is available in “/Document Commons/Packages,” invoke a tertiary Installer provided with the Package Reference. This will then invoke the main Package installer that is located in the Package’s Manifest.
RuleDisabled: This should always be true, except that when installing a new “Document Commons” container, this will be set to false (by the OnPaste action) in order to execute the included Rule only once. The Rule invokes the “Installer” Action Note that is normally the first child of this “Essentials” container.
Before the Rule for this “Add-on Packages” container is invoked by the “Essentials” Rule, the values for these two attributes will be set as follows:
	•	MyBoolean: The “Document Commons” container’s $OnPaste action will set this to true if there is already a “Document Commons” container as the last sibling of the cover. 
	•	MyNumber: The $ID of the correct “Document Commons” container. This could either be the parent of this “Essentials” container, or it could be the ID of an already existing “Document Commons.”
The Rule for this “Add-on Packages” container will assign for each of the included Package Reference notes the designated values for these two attributes:
	•	MyNumber: The $ID of the correct “Document Commons” container. This is just copied from the value passed from the “Essentials” Rule.
	•	MyString: The Path string to the correct “InstallerLog” note where subsequent log messages should be posted.</text>
