<attribute name="Subtitle" >Debugging &amp; Logging Tools</attribute>
<attribute name="Width" >3</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >14</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >Package and Version information
Package name: Logging tools
Parent Document: Toolbox
Package version: 2.0.3
Tinderbox version used: 10.1.2 (b711)
Minimum Tinderbox version: 9.1

User Attributes:
	•	$LoggingEnabled	boolean	If true (checked), logging is enabled
	•	$IndexLogs	boolean	If true (checked), Indexes prepended
	•	$DatestampLogs	boolean	If true (checked), Date stamp prepended
	•	$TimestampLogs	boolean	If true (checked), Time stamp prepended
	•	$SafePath	string	An escaped version of the $Path attribute
Containers and Notes:
	•	Document Commons—Last Top-level container
	⁃	LogBooks—Container where log books will be placed
	⁃	PersistentLogBook—A persistent log book used for historical event records
	•	Prototypes—System Container for prototypes (there should only be one in the document)
	⁃	Function—Prototype for functions based on Action Prototype 
	⁃	Log Book—Prototype for document log books
	⁃	Persistent Log Book—Prototype that is a child prototype of Log Book. Log books set to use this prototype will not be deleted by the “Delete Log Books” stamp
	•	Hints—System Container where Stamps and Code Library reside
	⁃	Stamps—Container for Stamp code notes 
	⁃	Logging:Stop Logging!—Turn off logging globally
	⁃	Logging:Bookmark Entry—Post a bookmark into StampLog book
	⁃	Logging:Stamp Log Entry—Record new log entry into StampLog book
	⁃	Logging:Restart Index Sequencing—Set master log index to zero
	⁃	Logging: Delete Log Books—Delete all non-persistent log books
	⁃	Library—System Container where Function code notes reside
	⁃	Record Log Entry—Code for LogRec(logbook, entry) function
	⁃	StopWatch—A simple stop watch function with a lap timer. 
</text>
