<attribute name="Subtitle" >Diagram View</attribute>
<attribute name="Width" >3</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >38.5</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >The preferred way to install the Diagram View package is to simply select the Copy of “Document Commons” container and paste it into the desired destination document. This will automatically install (nearly) everything necessary to use this Package. This same approach can be used to update the Diagram View package in documents where it was previously installed. For more details, review this ReadMe.
At this time, it is not possible for the automated installation procedure to fully define the two required Link Types: 
	Diagram←Note
	Diagram_Reflection→Note 
However, these two Link Types should be present in the destination document, but they  will need to be configured manually as follows:
	•	Diagram←Note Use the Document Inspector to bring up the Links tab as shown below with the “Diagram←Note” Link type selected.  ￼ Uncheck the “visible” and “labeled” options, and then enter this text into the “Action” field: 	action($Text(&quot;/Hints/Link «Reflect Note into Diagram»&quot;)); 
	•	Diagram_Reflection→Note  Select the “Diagram_Reflection→Note” Link type, and uncheck the “visible” and “labeled” check boxes as shown here: ￼ This completes configuration of the two required Link types for the Diagramming package to work correctly.

</text>
