<attribute name="URL" >https://acrobatfaq.com/atbref10/index/Automating_Tinderbox/Coding/Use_of_Attributes/Attribute_Listings/System_Attribute_Groups_within_Tinderbox/Appearance_Attributes.html</attribute>
<attribute name="Width" >3</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >28</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >Appearance 
	AccentColor	color	Specifies an alternate color used in patterns that overlay the $Color background of a note. Also used as the accent color for bar graphs.
	Badge	string	Specifies which badge icon should be used for a note.
	BadgeMonochrome	boolean	When true and $Color is dark, the badge appearance will be adjusted to be more visible.
	BadgeSize	number	If zero, then the default badge size (32 x 32 pixels) will be used. Otherwise, this attribute sets the square pixel count for a displayed badge.
	Border	number	If zero, then no border will be drawn for notes, containers, agents, and adornments. Otherwise, this specifies the stroke width for drawn borders. This corresponds to the “Width” control in the Appearance Inspector.
	BorderBevel	string	Can be set to none (no border drawn), plain (border is a simple line), raised (a beveled appearance is applied to border), and automatic. If set to automatic, then the border of a note will be beveled, while the border of an adornment will be plain. Set by Appearance Inspector Style control.
	BorderColor	color	Specifies the color used to draw a border.
	BorderDash	number	If zero, then no dashes will appear in borders. Otherwise, the value set the length of dashes drawn with the border.
	CaptionAlignment	string	Specifies how to align the text contained in $Caption as left, center, or right. This can be set in the Text Inspector.
	CaptionColor	color	Sets the color for $Caption text. Default is blue. 
	CaptionFont	font	Specifies the font for $Caption text. Default is “SketchnoteSquare.”
	CaptionOpacity	number	Sets opacity for a caption. Must be a value between zero (0) and one (1). Default is 1, which is fully opaque.
	CaptionSize	number	Specified as a percentage (0% to 100%) of $TextFontSize.
	Color	color	Specifies the color of adornments and notes. Default is blue for adornments and 7 for notes. This attribute also sets the color of notes in other views, including the Outline view.
	Color2	color	Deprecated attribute
	Flags	list	Specifies which flag to display with a note.
	Opacity	number	Sets the opacity for notes in Map view. Must be a value between zero (0) and one (1). Default is 1, which is fully opaque.
	Pattern	string	Used to specify use of patterns and gradients that alternate between $Color and $AccentColor for the background of notes (and adornments?). This can be set via Appearance Inspector, or by manual editing of attribute value.  Manual edits are used for graphs and plots. Default is plain, which indicates no pattern will be shown.
	PlotColor	color	Specifies color to be used when drawing plots in containers. Can be set via the Appearance Inspector.
	Shadow	boolean	If true, then a drop shadow will be shown for a note displayed in Map view. Default is false. 
	ShadowBlur	number	Determines how much to blur (or fog) a shadow. Allowed range is 0 – 100, with the default at 10.
	ShadowColor	color	Color used to draw shadow for note.
	ShadowDistance	number	Offset applied to shadows drawn for a note. Allowed range is 0 – 100, with the default at 5.
	Shape	string	Specifies which shape to draw for a note. Allowed values are normal, rectangle, oval, diamond, tag, vertical tag, bubble, hex, lozenge, cloud, leaf, banner, and arrow. 
General		
	AdornmentCount	number	
	Aliases	list	Aside: A similar approach could be used for Diagrams 
	Caption	string	Caption text displayed beneath notes in Map view.
	Checked	boolean	
	ChildCount	number	
	ClusterTerms	set	A set of text words that will be presented as terms that will be clustered with an adornment when force-directed layout (a.k.a., ‘Dance’) is invoked.
	Container	string	
	Created	date	
	CreatedFrom	string	
	Creator	string	
	DescendantCount	number	
	DisplayExpression	action	Action code that can customize the way a note’s name is displayed in various views. The result of code execution is text in $DisplayName, which is what will be shown in place of the normal display of $Name. Use of this feature can be disabled via $DisplayExpressionDisabled.
	DisplayExpressionDisabled	boolean	
	DisplayName	string	This is the text string that will be displayed in place of $Name. Since this is the result of executing $DisplayExpression, this cannot be set manually, and it appears to be read-only.
	Edict	action	Action code that is run as an edict rule for a note.
	EdictDisabled	boolean	If true, the edict rule will not be executed periodically for a note. Default is false. 
	File	file	
	HoverBackgroundColor	color	Sets background color of a hover pop-up.
	HoverExpression	action	Action code that determines what will be displayed by a hover pop-up.
	HoverImage	file	Indicates a file containing an image that will be displayed as part of a hover pop-up.
	HoverOpacity	number	Specifies the opacity for a hover pop-up. Must be a value between zero (0) and one (1). Default is 0.5, which is half-way opaque.
	ID	number	Unique ID number for note that can be used to reference note absolutely no matter where it is located in the overall Tinderbox document. The ID value is unique within a document, and will be changed if the note is copied to another document.
	IDString	string	A unique string that can be used as an alternative way to absolutely reference a note within a Tinderbox document. This may also have use when referring to notes from other applications. Each $IDstring is prefixed with “tbx:” to be followed by a random string unique to the note.
	InboundLinkCount	number	
	IsAction	boolean	
	IsAdornment	boolean	read-only
	IsAlias	boolean	read-only
	IsPrototype	boolean	
	LocalAttributes	set	A set comprising the attributes that are not inherited for a note, and thus considered ‘local’ to the note.
	Modified	date	Indicates the date/time that the $Text of a note was last modified.
	Name	string	Used as the normally displayed title of a note, as well as for referencing the note within the overall Tinderbox document. 
	OnAdd	action	Action code associated with a container that will be executed when a new child is added to the container.
	OnRemove	action	Action code associated with a container that will be executed when a child note is removed from the container.
	OutboundLinkCount	number	read-only
	OutlineDepth	number	read-only
	OutlineOrder	number	read-only
	Path	string	read-only
	PlainLinkCount	number	Count of plain, or basic, outbound links for a note, as distinguished from text or web links. read-only
	Private	boolean	If true, and if the note is a Prototype, then it will not appear in menus or pop-up lists. Effectively, this hides the Prototype from user selection/application via the UIs.
	Prototype	string	Reference to a note’s Prototype, if any. An empty string indicates no Prototype.
	PrototypeBequeathsChildren	boolean	If true, the children of a Prototype will be inherited by notes using that Prototype. Default is true. This should be set to false for a Prototype is itself a container with other Prototypes.
	ReadCount	number	Deprecated
	Rule	action	Action code executed as the rule for a note. 
	RuleDisabled	boolean	If true, the note’s rule will not execute automatically. Default value is false, implying that the rule will run periodically.
	Searchable	boolean	If false, the note will be excluded from searches. Default is true.  Aside: Diagram notes should perhaps default to false. 
	SelectionCount	number	
	SiblingOrder	number	Ordinal of the sibling within a parent context. First sibling is ‘1’.
	Subtitle	string	Text of note’s subtitle that is displayed beneath the title ($Name or $DisplayName) in Map view
	TextLinkCount	number	read-only
	WebLinkCount	number	read-only
Grid (for Adornments only)		
	GridColor	color	The color of grid lines and text on an adornment.
	GridColumns	number	The number of columns in an adornment grid.
	GridLabelFont	fort	The font to be used for an adornment’s grid labels.
	GridLabels	list	A list of labels for columns, then rows in a grid. These labels will be shown at the bottom of each grid cell.
	GridLabelSize	number	The size of text in labels displayed with an adornment’s grid.
	GridOpacity	number	Specifies the opacity for an adornment’s grid lines and text. Must be a value between zero (0) and one (1). Default is 0.75, which is 3/4 opaque.
	GridRows	number	The number of rows in an adornment grid.
Map		
	AdornmentFont	font	The font used to display text in adornments. If this is an empty value, then $NameFont will determine the font used for the adornment.
	Base	number	A number between 0 and 1 that is used to control the shape of notes that are arrows or leaves. Default value is 0.5.
	Bend	number	A number between -1 to +1 used to control how much a banner or leaf shape is bent. Default value is zero.
	Direction	boolean	For notes using shapes that indicate a direction, this specifies which direction.
	Fill	file	Specifies a file that provides an image to be displayed as the background for notes and adornments.
	FillOffsetY	number	Used to move the $Fill image vertically. There is no corresponding attribute for horizontal (X) movement. The value is in map units, where a negative number moves up.
	FillOpacity	number	Opacity for the $Fill image displayed in the background of a note or adornment in Map view. Must be a value between zero (0) and one (1). Default is 0.75, which is 3/4 opaque.
	Height	number	Height of a note or adornment in Map view expressed in map units. Used with $Width to specify the overall size within a Map view.
	HoverFont	font	The font used to display a $HoverExpression pop-up.
	InteriorScale	number	Used as a magnification factor to scale down objects displayed within a container in Map view. Default value is 1.5. 
	LeafBase	number	Deprecated, use $Base instead.
	LeafBend	number	Deprecated, use $Bend instead.
	LeafDirection	boolean	Deprecated, use $Direction instead.
	LeafTip	number	Deprecated, use $Tip instead.
	Lock	boolean	If true, then the position of a note or adornment in Map view cannot be changed. I.e., it is locked in place. 
	MapBackgroundAccentColor	color	
	MapBackgroundColor	color	
	MapBackgroundColor2	color	Deprecated
	MapBackgroundFill	string	
	MapBackgroundFillOpacity	number	
	MapBackgroundPattern	string	
	MapBackgroundShadow	boolean	
	MapBodyTextColor	color	
	MapBodyTextSize	number	
	MapNameSize	number	
	MapScrollX	number	
	MapScrollY	number	
	MapTextSize	number	Deprecated
	NameAlignment	string	Specifies horizontal alignment of title and subtitle in notes and adornments as left, center, or right.
	NameBold	boolean	Indicates if note name should be shown in a bold face.
	NameColor	color	Sets the color used to display the title of a note in Map view.
	NameFont	font	Font used to display the $Name text for notes in Map, Outline, and other views. This setting will also be the default for an adornment that has an empty value for $AdornmentFont.
	NameLeading	number	Specify leading between lines if a note title spans multiple lines. Default value is zero. If set to -1 the $NameFont establishes leading.
	NameOpacity	number	Specifies opacity for displaying the note’s name in Map view. Must be a value between zero (0) and one (1). Default is 1, which is fully opaque.
	NameStrike	boolean	Display note title in strike-through if true. 
	NameVerticalAlignment	string	Specifies vertical alignment of title and subtitle in notes and adornments as top, center, or bottom.
	PlotBackgroundColor	color	
	PlotBackgroundOpacity	number	Opacity for background display of a plot container in Map view. Must be a value between zero (0) and one (1). Default is 0.5, which is half opaque.
	PlotColorList	list	List of colors to be used for a pie chart.
	Sticky	boolean	If true, then any notes containers, agents, or other adornments that overlap this adornment will move with the adornment in Map view. Aside: This could be a partial solution to object grouping in Diagrams.
	Stripe	number	Specifies width of an optional vertical stripe on right side of note in Map view. Default value is zero, which results in no stripe.
	StripeColor	color	Determines color for a stripe if drawn.
	SubtitleColor	color	Color used to display subtitles in Map view. Default is automatic, which means that the subtitle will use $NameColor.
	SubtitleOpacity	number	Opacity used to display subtitle. Must be a value between zero (0) and one (1). Default is 0.5, which is half opaque.
	SubtitleSize	number	Size of subtitle display in Map view expressed as a percentage of the text size used for Name display.
	TableExpression	action	Used to construct summary displays in Table view for containers. 
	TableHeading	string	Specifies column headings in Table view.
	Tip	number	Controls shape of arrow and leaf shapes for notes. 
	TitleHeight	number	Sets the height in map units for the title bar in containers and agents in Map view. 
	TitleOpacity	number	Opacity used to display title (e.g., Name). Must be a value between zero (0) and one (1). Default is 1, which is fully opaque.
	Width	number	Width of a note or adornment in Map view expressed in map units. Used with $Height to specify the overall size within a Map view.
	Xpos	number	Specifies placement along x-axis of object in Map view in map units. 
	Ypos	number	Specifies placement along y-axis of object in Map view in map units. 
Net		
	AutoFetch	boolean	
	AutoFetchCommand	action	
	LastFetched	date	
	NoteURL	string	A read-only attribute that provides a Tinderbox URL that other applications can use to reference the note. The URL is of the form “tinderbox://…” and can be used by applications like DEVONthink to refer back to copied Tinderbox notes.
	RawData	string	Experimental
	RSSChannelTemplate	file	Deprecated
	RSSItemLimit	number	Deprecated
	RSSItemTemplate	file	Deprecated
	URL	URL	Provides URL string to be used when the current note fetches web content.
	ViewInBrowser	boolean	If true, then Tinderbox will automatically attempt to access the URL in $URL when the note is selected. Default is false. 
Outline		
	IsSeparator	boolean	Preferred setting to cause a note to appear as a separator in Outline view listings.
	MapPrototypeColor	color	Deprecated
	OutlineBackgroundColor	color	Color to be used as background of a selected note.
	OutlineColorSwatch	boolean	Deprecated
	OutlineNameSize	number	Determines relative size of note title text in Outline, Chart, and Timeline views.
	OutlineTextSize	number	Deprecated, use OutlineNameSize instead.
	PrototypeHighlightColor	color	Set the color used for the circle shading shown for Prototypes in Outline view listings.
	Separator	boolean	Equivalent to $IsSeparator, which is the preferred way to cause a note to be presented as a separator in Ouline view listings.
Places		
	Address	string	
	City	string	
	Country	string	
	District	string	
	FormattedAddress	string	Deprecated
	GeocodedAddress	string	
	Latitude	number	
	Longitude	number	
	PostalCode	string	
	Range	number	Can be used to set the range covered by an adornment in kilometers. This would probably be used to place map images into Map view with some facility to scale.
	State	string	
Sandbox		
	MyBoolean		
	MyColor		
	MyDate		
	MyDictionary		
	MyInterval		
	MyList		
	MyNumber		
	MySet		
	MyString
TextFormat		
	AutomaticIndent	boolean	Deprecated
	CodeFont	font	
	DisplayedAttributes	list	List of attributes to be displayed attributes table. This is only relevant in Outline view or text panes.
	DisplayedAttributesDateFormat	string	String used to specify format for dates in displayed attributes table.
	DisplayedAttributesFont	font	
	DisplayedAttributesFontSize	number	
	HideDisplayedAttributes	boolean	
	HideKeyAttributes	boolean	Deprecated
	HideTitle	boolean	Indicates if note’s title and subtitle should be hidden in Map view.
	ImageSizeLimit	number	Maximum size for images placed within $Text.
	KeyAttributeDateFormat	string	Deprecated
	KeyAttributeFont	font	Deprecated
	KeyAttributeFontSize	number	Deprecated
	KeyAttributes	set	Deprecated
	LeftMargin	string	Deprecated. Legacy method for setting left margin.
	LineSpacing	number	Line spacing within paragraphs.
	NoSpellling	boolean	If true, spell checking will not be performed for note. Default is false. 
	ParagraphSpacing	number	Line spacing between paragraphs.
	QuickListHangingIndent	number	
	QuickListIndent	number	
	RightMargin	string	Deprecated. Legacy method for setting right margin.
	ShowTitle	boolean	Deprecated
	SmartLinks	boolean	When true, URLs will be automatically recognized within $Text. Default is true. 
	SmartQuotes	boolean	Determines whether smart quote conversions should be performed for note’s text. Default is true, which means smart quotes will be used.
	SyntaxHighlighting	string	Default is empty string, meaning no highlighting.
	Tabs	string (list)	This is a semicolon-separated list of tab stops for the Text pane ruler. 
	TextAlign	string	Deprecated
	TextBackgroundColor	color	Background color assignment for text displayed for map objects in Map view.
	TextColor	color	Sets default (starting) color for $Text shown in text view panes.  Aside: This is awkward to use in practice. Seek alternative methods.
	TextColorBlue	color	
	TextColorGray	color	
	TextColorGreen	color	
	TextColorRed	color	
	TextFont	font	Initial font used for displaying text.
	TextFontSize	number	Initial font size used for displaying text.
	TextHighlightBlue	color	
	TextHighlightGreen	color	
	TextHighlightMagenta	color	
	TextHighlightRed	color	
	TextHighlightYellow	color	
	TextPaneRatio	number	Deprecated
	TextPaneWidth	number	Deprecated
	TextSidebar	boolean	Deprecated
	TextWindowHeight	number	
	TextWindowWidth	number	
	TitleBackgroundColor	color	Deprecated
	TitleFont	font	Deprecated
	TitleForegroundColor	color	Deprecated
	Ziplinks	boolean	If true, the Ziplinks method can be used to create text links. Default is true. 



Map Configuration		
	AdornmentFont		
	ClusterTerms		
