<attribute name="Name" >Introductory article on Diagram View by &quot;Perplexity&quot;</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenHeight" >23</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenWidth" >679</attribute>
<attribute name="SelectionCount" >5</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >2.483526866e-09</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >-0.4;-0.8;-0.2;0.8;0.6;0</attribute>
<attribute name="Subtitle" >Diagram View</attribute>
<attribute name="Width" >3</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >0</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >Jeremy Wagstaff offered this feedback on “Diagram View”
I read with interest your post on Diagram View. Not having used Tinderbox for a while I found your approach interesting but struggled to get my head around some parts of it, so I asked Perplexity to have a go at an introductory document, which is attached. I am sending it over;  just thought it might be of interest—and I&apos;m sure it&apos;s wrong in several places!
Actually, the Perplexity summary is surprisingly good, and I did not notice any errors. Jeremy provided this public link to the Perplexity-generated introductory document:
https://www.perplexity.ai/page/understanding-the-new-diagram-Gwf_biWMTXin1iEZJpLcfQ
Sometimes, AI can produce quite useful assessments.</text>
