<attribute name="DisplayedAttributes" >Subtitle;Caption;MyString;MyBoolean;MyNumber;MySet;MyDictionary;MyDate;Creator;Created;Modified;Checked;EdictDisabled;RuleDisabled</attribute>
<attribute name="DominantLanguage" >en</attribute>
<attribute name="Edict" >action($Text(&quot;/Hints/Edict «Attribute Note»&quot;));</attribute>
<attribute name="Modified" >2025-04-05T15:31:22+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="MyDate" >2025-02-20T22:32:54+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="MyDictionary" >category:User;sequential:;lines:2;readonly:;type:set;description:A set of Link Types that are allowed to be displayed in a diagram are kept in this attribute. It defaults to the Tinderbox-defined set of Link Types, but it can be extended to include user-defined Link Types, or to exclude standard Tinderbox Link Types. This attribute is associated with Diagram Containers, and when links are reflected into a diagram, this set determines which links are allowed to be reflected.



































;suggested:;default:agree;clarify;disagree;example;exception;note;response;update</attribute>
<attribute name="MyNumber" >2</attribute>
<attribute name="MyString" >agree;clarify;disagree;example;exception;note;response;update</attribute>
<attribute name="NLNames" >Link Types</attribute>
<attribute name="Name" >Reflected_LinkTypes</attribute>
<attribute name="Rule" >action($Text(&quot;/Hints/Edict «Attribute Note»&quot;));$Checked=false;$RuleDisabled=true;</attribute>
<attribute name="RuleDisabled" >true</attribute>
<attribute name="SafePath" >/Document Commons/Document Attributes/Reflected_LinkTypes</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenHeight" >23</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenWidth" >679</attribute>
<attribute name="SelectionCount" >38</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >-0.6000000238</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >-0.6;-0.6</attribute>
<attribute name="Subtitle" >set</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >129.5</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >A set of Link Types that are allowed to be displayed in a diagram are kept in this attribute. It defaults to the Tinderbox-defined set of Link Types, but it can be extended to include user-defined Link Types, or to exclude standard Tinderbox Link Types. This attribute is associated with Diagram Containers, and when links are reflected into a diagram, this set determines which links are allowed to be reflected.




































</text>
</item>
<item ID="1744596742" Creator="Chuck Wade" >
<attribute name="Badge" >information</attribute>
<attribute name="Caption" >User Attribute updated from this Note at 26-01-03 11:01:30</attribute>
<attribute name="Checked" >true</attribute>
<attribute name="Color" >#009193</attribute>
<attribute name="Created" >2025-03-21T12:41:34+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="DisplayedAttributes" >Subtitle;Caption;MyString;MyBoolean;MyNumber;MySet;MyDictionary;MyDate;Creator;Created;Modified;Checked;EdictDisabled;RuleDisabled</attribute>
<attribute name="DominantLanguage" >en</attribute>
<attribute name="Edict" >action($Text(&quot;/Hints/Edict «Attribute Note»&quot;));</attribute>
<attribute name="Modified" >2025-04-05T15:31:22+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="MyDictionary" >category:User;sequential:;lines:1;readonly:;type:dictionary;description:A dictionary of all outbound, plain, visible links from the associated note. The dictionary key:value pairs are “destID:type” where “destID” is the $ID of the destination link and “type” is a list of link types. Normally, there will only be one member for the link type list, but it is possible to have multiple links between the same two notes as long as the link types are not the same. When a note is reflected into a Diagram container, then it will have this dictionary created automatically. Similarly, the associated “reflection note” in the Diagram will have a corresponding dictionary but only for links that are reflected into the Diagram, which means that the destIDs will be for reflection notes within the Diagram.












;suggested:;default:</attribute>
<attribute name="MyNumber" >1</attribute>
<attribute name="Name" >Reflected_Links</attribute>
<attribute name="Rule" >action($Text(&quot;/Hints/Edict «Attribute Note»&quot;));$Checked=false;$RuleDisabled=true;</attribute>
<attribute name="RuleDisabled" >true</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenHeight" >22</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenWidth" >679</attribute>
<attribute name="SelectionCount" >16</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >-0.5000000149</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >-0.4;-0.6</attribute>
<attribute name="Subtitle" >dictionary</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >147</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >A dictionary of all outbound, plain, visible links from the associated note. The dictionary key:value pairs are “destID:type” where “destID” is the $ID of the destination link and “type” is a list of link types. Normally, there will only be one member for the link type list, but it is possible to have multiple links between the same two notes as long as the link types are not the same. When a note is reflected into a Diagram container, then it will have this dictionary created automatically. Similarly, the associated “reflection note” in the Diagram will have a corresponding dictionary but only for links that are reflected into the Diagram, which means that the destIDs will be for reflection notes within the Diagram.













</text>
</item>
</item>
