<item ID="1744856049" Creator="Chuck Wade" proto="Task" >
<attribute name="Created" >2025-02-26T14:45:29+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="DisplayedAttributes" >Subtitle;Creator;Modified;StartDate;EndDate</attribute>
<attribute name="DominantLanguage" >en</attribute>
<attribute name="Height" >1.86</attribute>
<attribute name="Modified" >2025-03-03T14:42:42+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="Name" >Add ability to snapshot a diagram</attribute>
<attribute name="SelectionCount" >21</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >-0.3000000119</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >0;-0.6</attribute>
<attribute name="StartDate" >2025-02-26T14:37:52+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="Subtitle" >Diagram View</attribute>
<attribute name="Width" >3</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >14</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >In this case, a “snapshot” would be a copy of an entire Diagram container, but with all child notes and links unreflected from the originals. In other words, future changes to notes in the main document would no longer be reflected into the snapshot. While there are several potential uses for snapshots, the primary motivation would be to create a Diagram that could be moved intact to some other Tinderbox document. </text>
