<attribute name="Name" >User Attributes</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenHeight" >23</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenWidth" >679</attribute>
<attribute name="SelectionCount" >47</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >-0.6666666766</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >-0.4;-0.6;-1</attribute>
<attribute name="Subtitle" >Network Tools</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >28</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >User Attribute notes located in this container will be moved to the “/Document Commons/Document Attributes” container as part of the installation procedure. The copies located here should have $Checked, $RuleDisabled, and $EdictDisabled all set to true. After moving these into the Document Attributes container, the Installer will set $RuleDisabled, and $EdictDisabled to false. The Rule will then execute once and set $RuleDisabled to true and $Checked to false. This will cause the associated User Attribute to be created if it does not already exist, and the settings from the Attribute Note will be applied to the User Attribute. 
Note that by leaving $Checked set to false, only the description of the corresponding User Attribute will be updated from the $Text of the Attribute Note via the Edict. The user can set $Checked true if they want to apply other settings from the Attribute Note to the actual User Attribute.</text>
