<attribute name="Telephone" >1642349249</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >45.4</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >-0.1</attribute>
<text >For future versions of this “Document Commons” framework, this might be where document configurations are kept (see Michael Becker’s TBXconfig as an example). Other packages that are later added to this framework are also likely to need specific containers and notes that support their intended purpose, much as this current version uses the “LogBooks” container to capture logging and provide necessary attributes and initial values. 
Examples of items that might be common to the members of a package include counters, indexes, lists, sets, lookup dictionaries, or color themes.
</text>
