<attribute name="Subtitle" >User Attribute Management</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >14</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >Package and Version information
Package name: Attribute Management
Parent Document: Toolbox
Package version: tbp
Tinderbox version used: 10.1.1 (b706)
Minimum Tinderbox version: 10.1

User Attributes:
By design, this package does not require any User Attributes. Instead, it makes use of existing System Attributes, including the Sandbox category. This is so that minimal effort is required to insert this package into another Tinderbox document.
Containers and Notes:
	•	Document Commons—Last Top-level container. It is recommended that this container be copied into the destination Tinderbox document since it includes an Edict to update the $MyDictionary(Document Commons) to provide an index of consistently-named children as well as a Rule that will force this container to always be the last top-level Note in the document where it resides.
	⁃	Document Attributes—Container where “Attribute Notes” are kept
	⁃	Children—These are the Attribute Notes. For the most part, these are automatically generated
	•	Hints—System Container where Stamps and Code Library reside The only code notes stored under “Hints” are for automation to generate and update Attribute Notes.
	⁃	Edict (Attribute Note)—Each Attribute Note’s Edict will invoke this code using:  action($Text(&quot;/Hints/Edict (Attribute Note)&quot;));
	⁃	OnVisit (Document Attributes)—The “Document Attributes” container utilizes its $OnVisit action to invoke: action($Text(&quot;/Hints/OnVisit (Document Attributes))&quot;));
	•	Prototypes—No Prototypes are used by this Package. This is by design. 
</text>
