<attribute name="Name" >ReadMe “Diagram View”</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenHeight" >23</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenWidth" >679</attribute>
<attribute name="SelectionCount" >45</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >-0.383333344</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >-0.2;-1;-0.6;-0.6;1;0.2;-0.8;-0.4;-0.6;-0.6;-0.2;-0.8</attribute>
<attribute name="Subtitle" >Diagram View</attribute>
<attribute name="Telephone" >+1 508 277-6439</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >24.5</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >This version of the “Diagram View” package has been substantially enhanced over the initial prototype provided earlier this year, and is now a fully developed Tinderbox application. Note that Tinderbox 10.2.0 or later is required. (The prior 10.1.2b710 released version does not work with this Diagram View.)
The most significant enhancements introduced with this version improve the way that links are reflected from the user’s main document into a Diagram. It is believed that all edge cases are now dealt with so that links are added and removed from a Diagram as changes are made within the main document. Also, any changes to a Diagram’s configuration or to link settings for any reflection objects that alter the way that links should be displayed will be handled correctly. Parallel links between the same two notes are now allowed, and will be reflected correctly into Diagrams. The new behaviors should be both intuitive and obvious to the user, even though what is going on under the hood is rather complex.
Two new stamps have been added to support another new feature that allows notes to added to a Diagram in bulk. The “Set Active Diagram” stamp merely indicates what Diagram is being updated, and the “Add Notes to Active Diagram” stamp will do just what it says for all currently selected notes. This is often the easiest way to set up a new Diagram, and some users may prefer this approach instead of the alternative method that uses a special link to add notes to Diagram containers. Both methods are supported in this release.
Documentation for this package is built into the “Diagram View” Package. The best starting point for understanding what Diagram Views in Tinderbox can be used for, and how to work with Diagrams is provided in this note:
	/Document Commons/Packages/Diagram Views/Overview of Diagram Views Package with a quick tutorial and examples
Details on how to add this package to your own Tinderbox documents is provided here:
	/Document Commons/Packages/Diagram Views/Deploying Diagram package to existing Tinderbox document
Please note that, while the installation of the Diagram View into a document is automated, it is still necessary at this time to tweak the configuration of two link types, as described in the above referenced note.
The “Playground” top-level container provided in this document includes a set of example notes that have been reflected into “Diagram A.” This would be a good place to start exploring how diagramming works with this package. Additional Diagram containers can be easily added to experiment with other diagramming examples. 
Feedback is welcome. 
Chuck Wade &lt;Chuck@Interisle.net&gt; +1 508 277-6439
</text>
