<attribute name="Subtitle" >Diagram View</attribute>
<attribute name="URL" >https://acrobatfaq.com/atbref10/index/Automating_Tinderbox/Coding/Use_of_Attributes/Attribute_Listings/System_Attribute_Groups_within_Tinderbox/Appearance_Attributes.html</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >28</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >Link reflections are managed by the UpdateDiagramLinks(diagram)function, which is called from the Diagram’s Edict. This function will scan all links from any note reflected into the Diagram, and then keep, add, or remove any links in the diagram to reflect the links in the main document. The CaptureOutboundPlainLinks(src_note) function is used to collect all outbound links from a reflected note into a dictionary that maps destination reflected notes to the corresponding link types. The same dictionary structure is used to capture the set of links that should be removed from a reflection object by calling the RemoveLinkSet(src_note,links2Remove:dictionary) function.
Criteria for a link to be reflected into a Diagram
	•	The link must connect two notes that are both reflected within the Diagram.
	•	Only basic links (i.e., not a URL and not an Anchor link) will be reflected into the Diagram.
	•	The link type must be “visible” for the link to be reflected into the Diagram.
	•	The Link Type must be on the list of allowed link reflections ($Reflected_LinkTypes). The default list is defined in the Diagram container, but can be overridden for any specific reflection object. The rule is, if $Reflected_LinkTypes is not defined for a reflection object in the Diagram, then the Diagram container will provide this list.
	•	Parallel links between the same two reflected notes in the main document should be reflected into the Diagram if allowed.
	•	For each reflection object in the Diagram, the $Reflected_Links dictionary comprises all of the links that are allowed and found within the user’s main document.
	•	The link type will determine how a link will appear in both the main document and the Diagram.
Reflected links will be removed from the Diagram under these circumstances:
	•	If either the source or destination reflected note is removed from the Diagram.
	•	If a link between two reflected notes is removed in the main document.
	•	If the link type is no longer visible. This could include a link type corresponding to parallel links.
	•	 If changes to $Reflected_LinkTypes removes the link type as allowed in the Diagram. This could include a link type corresponding to parallel links.
Links can be added directly to a Diagram in an ad hoc manner. Such links have no reflected counterpart, and thus do not appear in the main document. 
	•	A link can be added directly between any two notes in the Diagram.  The Diagram notes can be reflections of notes in the user’s main document, or they can be unreflected notes.
	•	Such ad hoc links can be of any type, but must be visible to be seen in the Diagram.
</text>
