<attribute name="SafePath" >/Document Commons/Packages/Diagram Views/Diagram tools Manifest</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenHeight" >23</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenWidth" >679</attribute>
<attribute name="SelectionCount" >97</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >-0.5360000098</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >-0.8;-0.2;-1;0.4;0;-0.6;-0.6;-0.8;-0.8;-0.6;-0.8;-1;-0.8;0.2;-0.6;-0.6;-0.2;-1;-0.6;-0.4;-0.6;-0.8;-0.2;0;-1</attribute>
<attribute name="Subtitle" >Diagram View</attribute>
<attribute name="Width" >3</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >17.5</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >User attributes: 
	•	Diagram_ID:  (number)  Always set to $ID for the Diagram Container. This is necessary for some action code used to maintain a diagram. Every child of a Diagram Container should have this attribute set to point to its parent, even though this is usually not necessary. If a note is removed from the Diagram Container, then this attribute will be set to zero.
	•	Reflected_ID: (number)  The $ID of the original source note that has been reflected into the Diagram. This is always available in each Reflection Object note.
	•	Reflected_Notes: (dictionary)  This is a dictionary maintained in each Diagram Container that maps the $IDs of Reflected Notes to the $IDs of the Reflection Objects.
	•	Reflected_LinkTypes: (set) Only Link Types included in this set will be reflected into the diagram. 
	•	DiagramAttributesReflection: (set) The set of appearance-oriented attributes that will be copied from the Reflected Note to the Reflection Object in the diagram. It is possible to add other attributes to this set that should be copied to the Reflection Object. Any of these attributes can be overridden by the “DiagramReflectionLocals” set (see below). The Diagram Container holds the default version of this set, but any Reflection Object can have its own version to allow further customization.
	•	DiagramReflectionLocals: (set) This is a set of attributes that will not be copied from the Reflected Note. This allows Reflection Objects to deviate from the original where desired.
Prototypes:
	•	Diagram: Prototype for Diagram Containers. This also sets OnAdd, OnRemove, Rule, and Edict actions. This Prototype has the following three Prototypes as subordinate children. 
	⁃	Reflection Object: Prototype assigned to child notes of the Diagram Container that will reflect original source notes into the diagram. This is set by the Link Create action for the “Diagram←Note” Link Type.
	⁃	Diagram Object: Any note added directly to the Diagram Container. This will be enforced by the Container’s OnAdd.
	⁃	Diagram Adornment: Any adornment added directly to the Diagram Container. This will be enforced by the Container’s OnAdd.
Action Code: 
	•	Link “Reflect Note into Diagram” This is the code that will execute every time a new link of Link type “Diagram←Note” is made to a “Diagram” container.
	•	OnRemove «Diagram Object Note» Whenever a child note is removed from a “Diagram” container, then this code will be executed. If the note being removed is a “Reflection Note,” then this code will remove the corresponding entry in the “Reflected_Notes” dictionary for the Diagram as well as the diagram links to and from the “Reflected Note.”
Stamps: 
	•	Links:Remove Link From This is used to remove links when Reflection Objects are removed from a diagram.
	•	Links:Remove Link To Optional at this time, but may be used in future versions.
Functions: 
	•	Update Diagram Note Reflections function: UpdateDiagramReflections
	•	Update Diagram Reflected Links function: UpdateDiagramLinks
	•	Copy select attributes between two notes function: CopyAttributeSet
	•	Record Log Entry function: LogRec function used for debugging. Separate documentation is included in “Toolbox” that explains how to install the logging capability.
Note that further technical documentation is embedded in each of the elemental items comprising the “Diagram Views” package.

</text>
