<attribute name="Edict" >action($Text(&quot;/Hints/Edict «Attribute Note»&quot;));</attribute>
<attribute name="Modified" >2025-04-05T15:31:22+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="MyDate" >2025-02-20T22:32:54+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="MyDictionary" >category:User;sequential:;lines:1;readonly:;type:number;description:Reflection object notes within a Diagram Container will keep the ID of the note they reflect in this attribute. If the reflected note is moved, $ReflectedID can be used to reference it no matter where it is relocated. Although the link from a reflection object note to the original reflected note can also provide access, some diagram maintenance activities may be easier to code using this attribute.

































;suggested:;default:0</attribute>
<attribute name="MyNumber" >1</attribute>
<attribute name="MyString" >0</attribute>
<attribute name="Name" >Reflected_ID</attribute>
<attribute name="Rule" >action($Text(&quot;/Hints/Edict «Attribute Note»&quot;));$Checked=false;$RuleDisabled=true;</attribute>
<attribute name="RuleDisabled" >true</attribute>
<attribute name="SafePath" >/Document Commons/Document Attributes/Reflected_ID</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenHeight" >23</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenWidth" >679</attribute>
<attribute name="SelectionCount" >23</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >-0.6000000238</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >-0.6;-0.6</attribute>
<attribute name="Subtitle" >number</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >126</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >Reflection object notes within a Diagram Container will keep the ID of the note they reflect in this attribute. If the reflected note is moved, $ReflectedID can be used to reference it no matter where it is relocated. Although the link from a reflection object note to the original reflected note can also provide access, some diagram maintenance activities may be easier to code using this attribute.


































</text>
</item>
