<item ID="1744855897" Creator="Chuck Wade" proto="Task" >
<attribute name="Created" >2025-03-03T14:42:54+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="DisplayedAttributes" >Subtitle;Creator;Modified;StartDate;EndDate</attribute>
<attribute name="DominantLanguage" >en</attribute>
<attribute name="EndDate" >2025-03-26T15:59:03+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="Height" >1.86</attribute>
<attribute name="Modified" >2025-04-09T15:08:08+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="Name" >Handle situation where links are deleted in main document</attribute>
<attribute name="SelectionCount" >36</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >-0.400000001</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >0;-1;-0.2</attribute>
<attribute name="StartDate" >2025-03-03T14:43:25+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="Subtitle" >Diagram View</attribute>
<attribute name="Width" >3</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >24.5</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >0</attribute>
<text >Deleting a link between reflected notes should result in that link no longer appearing in any associated diagram. At least, not as a reflection. Question: should users still be able to add links that exist only in their diagram? How should such ad hoc diagram links be identified as not being link reflections?
3/27/25: This should be fully implemented in Toolbox 2.0.3c, though parallel links will require an update to Tinderbox. Many edge cases with links have also been resolved with this update. The “UpdateDiagramLinks(diagram)” function has been substantially reworked and is now much more complex.
</text>
